WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.667 --> 00:00:17.261
When Fraulein left Heidi's room, Heidi broke into a wild fit of weeping.

2
00:00:17.262 --> 00:00:21.901
"Now Grannie's rolls are all gone!" she cried.

3
00:00:21.902 --> 00:00:27.909
"They were all for Grannie and now they are all gone!"

4
00:00:27.910 --> 00:00:31.001
Clara was distressed at Heidi's tears.

5
00:00:31.002 --> 00:00:36.209
"Heidi, Heidi, please don't cry!" she said desperately.

6
00:00:36.210 --> 00:00:42.188
"I promise that when you go home, you shall have as many fresh rolls for Grannie as you want.

7
00:00:42.189 --> 00:00:45.042
Yours would have been hard and dry by then.

8
00:00:45.043 --> 00:00:48.387
Please, Heidi, don't cry anymore."

9
00:00:48.389 --> 00:00:54.539
Clara's promise comforted Heidi a little, but she did not stop sobbing for a long time.

10
00:00:54.540 --> 00:00:58.971
When she arrived at supper, her eyes were still red from crying.

11
00:00:58.972 --> 00:01:04.419
She sat quietly at the table and tried her best to be well behaved.

12
00:01:04.420 --> 00:01:10.533
Whenever Sebastian caught her eye, he pointed strangely to his head and then to hers.

13
00:01:10.534 --> 00:01:13.814
Heidi couldn't understand what he was trying to tell her.

14
00:01:13.815 --> 00:01:21.019
But when she went to bed that night, she found her old straw hat under her bedspread.

15
00:01:21.020 --> 00:01:24.333
She snatched it up with delight and hugged it.

16
00:01:24.334 --> 00:01:30.280
Then she wrapped a handkerchief around it and hid it as far back in her cupboard as she could.

17
00:01:30.281 --> 00:01:38.814
A few mornings later, there was a great commotion and much running up and down the stairs in the large house.

18
00:01:38.815 --> 00:01:45.634
Clara's father had just returned with packages and boxes and lots of pretty things.

19
00:01:45.635 --> 00:01:49.353
When he arrived, he immediately went to see Clara.

20
00:01:49.354 --> 00:01:52.149
Heidi was sitting beside her in the study.

21
00:01:52.150 --> 00:01:56.522
Father and daughter hugged each other with warm affection.

22
00:01:56.523 --> 00:02:01.140
Then, Herr Sesemann held out his hand to Heidi and said kindly,

23
00:02:01.141 --> 00:02:03.931
"So this is our little Swiss girl.

24
00:02:03.932 --> 00:02:05.742
Come and shake hands with me!

25
00:02:05.743 --> 00:02:09.029
Now tell me, are Clara and you good friends?"

26
00:02:09.030 --> 00:02:13.588
"Yes, Clara is very kind to me," answered Heidi.

27
00:02:13.589 --> 00:02:18.492
He stayed and talked with the girls for a few minutes, and then they left to eat supper.

28
00:02:18.493 --> 00:02:24.085
Fraulein sat across from him at the table, her face sour with bad news.

29
00:02:24.086 --> 00:02:32.129
"Herr Sesemann, if you only knew the things Heidi has done─or the people and animals she has brought into this house!

30
00:02:32.130 --> 00:02:35.656
Her behavior is past understanding!"

31
00:02:35.657 --> 00:02:40.020
Clara's father listened to Fraulein, and he spoke with the tutor as well.

32
00:02:40.021 --> 00:02:41.868
Finally, he went to Clara.

33
00:02:41.869 --> 00:02:44.483
"And now, my dear little Clara,"

34
00:02:44.484 --> 00:02:48.959
he said, pulling up his chair and taking her hand in his.

35
00:02:48.960 --> 00:02:52.505
"What kind of animals has Heidi brought into the house?

36
00:02:52.506 --> 00:02:56.879
And why does Fraulein think that she is not in her right mind?"

37
00:02:56.880 --> 00:02:59.530
Clara had no difficulty explaining.

38
00:02:59.531 --> 00:03:03.304
She told her father about the kittens and the organ boy.

39
00:03:03.305 --> 00:03:06.346
Herr Sesemann laughed heartily and asked,

40
00:03:06.347 --> 00:03:09.179
"So do you want me to send Heidi home?"

41
00:03:09.180 --> 00:03:12.430
"Oh, no, no!" Clara exclaimed.

42
00:03:12.431 --> 00:03:14.700
"Please do not send her away."

43
00:03:14.701 --> 00:03:18.095
"It is settled then," said her father.

44
00:03:18.096 --> 00:03:21.453
Herr Sesemann was only home for a short time.

45
00:03:21.454 --> 00:03:28.241
He comforted Clara with the promise that Clara's Grandmamma would arrive soon to keep her company.

46
00:03:28.242 --> 00:03:32.686
Clara was overjoyed, and she told Heidi all about her.

47
00:03:32.687 --> 00:03:39.135
Upon her arrival, Clara's Grandmamma was eager to meet Heidi and welcomed her warmly.

48
00:03:39.136 --> 00:03:43.701
When Clara took her nap that afternoon, Grandmamma asked Fraulein,

49
00:03:43.702 --> 00:03:45.446
"Where is Heidi?

50
00:03:45.447 --> 00:03:48.822
And what does she do in the afternoons?"

51
00:03:48.823 --> 00:03:53.127
"She is sitting in her room, Frau Sesemann," said Fraulein.

52
00:03:53.128 --> 00:03:56.964
"Bring her to my room," said Grandmamma cheerfully.

53
00:03:56.965 --> 00:04:05.664
"I have some pretty books with me that I would like to give her."
